; Linux PIC code (ABI.md "Dynamic linking"): a symbol that is not dso_local
; comes from its GOT entry, `leapc rD, %gotpcrel(sym)` and an 8-byte load
; that is invariant and dereferenceable (MachineCSE shares it, MachineLICM
; takes it out of a loop).  An offset is added after the load (into the
; access), never into the relocation.  dso_local symbols stay `leapc sym`
; (a definition that a shared library exports through its local alias,
; `.Lsym$local`); an extern_weak one may resolve to 0, so it is not local.
; Other triples (BARE) keep PIC code without a GOT whatever dso_local says,
; and code that is not PIC (STATIC) is unchanged.

@ext = external global i32
@arr = external global [100 x i32]
@def = global i32 5
@loc = dso_local global i32 6
@hid = hidden global i32 7
@weakhid = extern_weak hidden global i32

